nterference in the formation of heterochromatin</article-title><source>Nature</source><volume>447</volume><fpage>399</fpage><lpage>406</lpage><year>2007</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17522672</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R13"><label>13</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Buhler</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Verdel</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Moazed</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Tethering RITS to a nascent transcript initiates RNAi- and heterochromatin-dependent gene silencing</article-title><source>Cell</source><volume>125</volume><fpage>873</fpage><lpage>886</lpage><year>2006</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16751098</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R14"><label>14</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nelson</surname><given-names>PT</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>A novel monoclonal antibody against human Argonaute proteins reveals unexpected characteristics of miRNAs in human blood cells</article-title><source>RNA</source><volume>13</volume><fpage>1787</fpage><lpage>1792</lpage><year>2007</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17720879</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R15"><label>15</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gilbert</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Kristjuhan</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Winkler</surname><given-names>GS</given-names></name><name><surname>Svejstrup</surname><given-names>JQ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Elongator interactions with nascent mRNA revealed by RNA immunoprecipitation</article-title><source>Mol Cell</source><volume>14</volume><fpage>457</fpage><lpage>464</lpage><year>2004</year><pub-id pub-